Also, because $\tan X = \frac{12}{b}$, $VW = \frac{12}{TV} = \frac{12(b)}{12} = b$.  Hence,
\begin{align*}
WY &= WX + XV + VY \\
&= b + b + (12 - b) \\
&= 12 + b.
\end{align*}Let the height of $WXZV$ from $W$ be $h$.  Then $\left[WXZV\right] = \frac{1}{2}(WX)(h) = \frac{1}{2}(b)(h)$.  Hence  \begin{align*}
\left[WXYZ\right] &= \left[WXZV\right] + \left[VWY\right] \\
&= \left[WXZV\right] + \frac{1}{2}(VW)(WY) \\
&= \left[\frac{1}{2}(b)(h) + \frac{1}{2}(b)(12 + b)\right] \\
&= \left[\frac{1}{2}(h + 6 + b)\right](b).
\end{align*}Then $\left[WXZV\right] = \frac{1}{2}(WX)(h) = \frac{1}{2}\left[\frac{1}{2}(b + 12)\right](h) = \frac{1}{4}(b + 12)(h)$.
Substituting these information, we obtain  \begin{align*}
